<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="measure"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Add a comparable measurement</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">nbn describes comparing speed tests beside the router, in other rooms and over Ethernet to the router where practical. It also identifies walls and other obstructions as possible influences on coverage. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://www.nbnco.com.au/learn/optimisation/what-to-look-for-in-a-wifi-router">See nbn's comparison guidance</a>.</p>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Keep equipment changes out of this check") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For the measurement steps and limits, use our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/connection-test-results/">connection-test guide</a>. Keep the time, device, connection type and test name with each result. Skip a wired comparison if it requires unfamiliar cabling or equipment changes.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="question"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Choose the next question</h2>
{% call note("info", "Good to know", "A pattern is not a diagnosis") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A room-specific pattern is useful to discuss when assessing coverage. A problem in several places needs a wider conversation. Neither pattern, by itself, proves which component has failed.</p>{% endcall %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Ask: “What would you check to distinguish the incoming service from the connection inside the house?” Bring the map rather than asking for a particular booster. If a provider investigates the service, keep its reference and findings so you do not lose that part of the history.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not compare a phone on mobile data with a laptop on home Wi-Fi and treat that as the same test. Our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-one-device-or-all/">one-device or all-devices guide</a> explains a fair comparison.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="notes"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Keep the useful result</h2>
{% call note("info", "Keep this", "An inconclusive result is still useful") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">You may finish with a clear pattern, an intermittent pattern or no repeatable problem. All three are worth recording. Do not turn an inconclusive test into a purchase decision. You can stop after a few representative observations; there is no need to test every corner of the house.</p>{% endcall %}

